  "steps": [
    "Rinse the lentils well. Put them in a saucepan with the water and 1 tsp salt, then bring to a boil and simmer for 18 to 22 minutes, until tender but still holding their shape.",
    "Drain the lentils well and spread them out for a few minutes so excess steam escapes and they cool slightly.",
    "Whisk together the olive oil, cider vinegar, mustard, garlic, black pepper, and 1/4 tsp salt to make the vinaigrette.",
    "Combine the lentils with the carrot, celery, red onion, and parsley in a bowl.",
    "Pour over the vinaigrette and toss well. Taste and adjust with a little more salt or vinegar if needed.",
    "Serve warm or at room temperature, letting the salad sit for 5 to 10 minutes for the flavours to meld."
